{%- comment -%}
  templates/index.liquid - Crema Italia storefront (POC3)

  A single-document SPA: every "page" below is a .page block, toggled client-side
  by showPage() in ci-storefront.js. Editorial copy is authored here in Liquid; the
  catalog grids, roaster profiles, product detail, cart and account views are filled
  at runtime from assets/ci-catalog.json (the baked-in test dataset).

  This renders only once Shopify password protection is OFF, or to a password-holder
  previewing the theme. While pre-launch, visitors still see templates/password.liquid.

  PROD: when the live store is built, the JS-rendered grids are replaced by
  real Liquid loops over {{ collection.products }} + crema_italia.* metafields, and the
  Roccia subscription UI binds to native selling_plan_groups (Loop). Integration points
  are flagged with <!-- LOOP --> / <!-- PROD --> comments.
{%- endcomment -%}

<!-- ============================== HOME ============================== -->
<!-- POC5 MODEL (2026-07-10, pending Steve's sign-off): story-first landing.
     Hero = questions -> payoff + single quiz CTA; sticky jump-chips; founder
     confession; model; shelves + contextual Sorpresa CTA; roasters; promise.
     Featured Tour removed from home; quiz is invitation-only (no auto-launch). -->
<div class="page active" id="page-home">
  {%- comment -%}
    POC30 item 1 (2026-09-12): the hero is IMAGE-FIRST. The B2C expert review of POC28 put "a
    product/sensory image in the first viewport" at the top of its Missing list: the hero was
    all copy and sold the operating model before creating any desire for the cup. Principle
    adopted from that review: the hero SEDUCES, the second screen JUSTIFIES. So a muted looping
    video of a pull landing on crema now comes first with ONE line over it, and the copy hero
    (claim, freshness mechanism, Benvenuto, quiz CTA) follows as the second band.
    The 300px knockout logo lockup came out of the hero at the same time - a cup lockup sitting
    on a photograph of a cup is redundant, the header already carries the logo, and "smaller
    logo, larger margins" is Brand Standards' own tie-breaker (CLAUDE.md section 12).
    PROD: photography slot 0 of 3 (hero). TEMPORARY MEDIA - ci-temp-hero.mp4 and
    ci-temp-hero-poster.jpg are stand-ins cut from Steve's own footage (MOV_3891, 2026-09-15,
    replacing the MOV_3863 take from POC30) and every ci-temp-* asset must be replaced before
    launch; the brief, and the three reasons this take is still a stand-in (a propped cup, a
    trademark cropped out of the left edge, tungsten light), are in docs/photography-todo.md.
    In production the hero is a video section with the media on Shopify Files (video_tag), not
    a theme asset.
    ACCESSIBILITY: muted + playsinline are what let it autoplay on iOS; the poster is the
    reduced-motion fallback (ci-storefront.js pauses the video when prefers-reduced-motion is
    set) and the first paint on slow connections. The video is decorative, so it carries no
    audio track and no captions; the only content is the H1 rendered as text over it.
    CONTRAST: cream on crema fails AA, so the H1 sits over an Espresso scrim (the palette's own
    hero tone at partial alpha - not a new colour) that fades to transparent across the frame.
  {%- endcomment -%}
