        <p>Steve Roberts is the founder of Crema Italia. His road to Italy is a long one - here is a brief recap, in his words:</p>
        <p>I am a dog person, but I&rsquo;ve lived a cat life. Meaning I&rsquo;m on life number six.</p>
        <div class="founder-lives">
          <p><strong>Life one.</strong> In pursuit of a professional music career as a French horn player - but my high C in Till Eulenspiegel was meek. Next.</p>
          <p><strong>Life two.</strong> I discovered computers, wrote a lot of custom software, and left the horn behind.</p>
          <p><strong>Life three.</strong> I founded a restaurant back-office company. It grew - and took me to Europe, then Italy, where I discovered espresso.</p>
          <p><strong>Life four.</strong> We sold the software business to a bigger one.</p>
          <p><strong>Life five.</strong> Retirement: family, kids, grandchildren, travel, mountain biking, flying airplanes, incredible new friends. Italy became my go-to place; Tuscany melts my heart (repeat, multiple times and counting).</p>
          <p><strong>Life six.</strong> <span class="ita">Allora</span> - the inspiration for Crema Italia. Two things in mind: bring amazing fresh coffee from amazing Italian roasters into the US, and help the people I love help me build it - so they can enjoy a few extra lives too.</p>
