    <h1>The Crema Italia Promise</h1>
  </div></div>
  <main class="ci-main">
    <ul class="promise-list">
      <li><div class="pn">1</div><div class="pt"><h3>Curated with love, never aggregated.</h3><p>A small group of Italian roasters - carefully chosen, not collected.</p></div></li>
      <li><div class="pn">2</div><div class="pt"><h3>Love your first bag, or we send a different one - free.</h3><p>Applies to every coffee on our three shelves.</p></div></li>
      <li><div class="pn">3</div><div class="pt"><h3>Cancel your subscription anytime in a couple of clicks.</h3><p>Pause, skip, swap, or cancel - all self-service, no minimum, no cancel fee.</p></div></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="prose" style="max-width:72ch">
      <h3>First-bag satisfaction guarantee</h3>
      <p>On any coffee from our three shelves, if your first bag is not right for you, we will send a different one - free. We would rather help you find your coffee than win an argument.</p>
      {%- comment -%}
        The "Offerta is different - sold as-is" guarantee used to be stated here as well as on
        the Offerta page (POC18 A6 named it as the one real duplicate on the site). With
        Offerta hidden (POC30 item 4) it is stated ONCE, on the page the invitation opens - a
