<!-- ============================== FAQ ============================== -->
<div class="page" id="page-faq">
  <main class="ci-main">
    <button class="back-btn" onclick="goBack()">&larr; Back</button>
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:0"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>FAQ</h2></div>
    <div class="prose" style="max-width:72ch">
      <h3>Do you sell ground coffee?</h3>
      <p>No. Whole beans offer you longer-lasting freshness, and a choice of grind (fine to coarse) to match your brewing preferences. You will always extract more of the coffee&rsquo;s taste and aroma by grinding just before brewing. If you need a grinder, look for a burr grinder in <button class="inline-link" onclick="showPage('bottega')">Accessories</button>.</p>
      <h3>How fresh is the coffee?</h3>
      <p>Every bag carries its roast date, and every coffee on our shelves shows the roast date of the oldest bag we hold, so the bag you receive is never older than the date you see. Most of the coffee on the market is sold with a 12 to 24 month shelf life, often described as &lsquo;Best by&rsquo; instead of an actual roast date. We remove beans from our shelves once the roast date is older than {{ settings.freshness_window_days }} days, to preserve the taste the roaster intended when they sealed the bag. Properly packaged coffee stays drinkable well beyond that, but we sell it only while it is at its freshest. Our policy is no waste: we will find a deserving home for the older coffee.</p>
      <h3>Do you roast the coffee?</h3>
      <p>No. We import and curate; the roasters roast. We never roast, blend, or repackage.</p>
      <h3>Is imported coffee regulated?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Every foreign food facility shipping to the U.S. must register with the FDA and name a U.S. Agent. We serve as that agent for our roaster partners.</p>
      <h3>How do subscriber discounts work?</h3>
      <p>An active subscription gives 10% off every coffee (Founding Members - the first {{ settings.founding_member_cap }} subscribers at launch - receive 12% for life). Accessories are never discounted. Discounts never stack: you always receive the single highest one you qualify for. A one-time first-purchase 5% applies only when it is your best rate, so a subscriber's first order still gets their 10%, or a Founding Member's 12%, whichever is higher, never both added together.</p>
      <h3>What goes in the discount code field at checkout?</h3>
      <p>Nothing. We do not issue promo/discount codes, to anyone, ever. No launch codes, no newsletter codes, no influencer codes. Any discount you have earned is calculated for you when you log in and check out.</p>
      <h3>How does gifting work?</h3>
      <p>Tick <strong>This order is a gift</strong> in your cart and add a short note. We print it on a card and put it in the box. Nothing inside any package we ship shows a price - gift or not - so there is nothing to remember and nothing to go wrong. Your receipt reaches you by email, never the box.</p>
      <p>Two things worth knowing. A gift ships to one address, so if you are buying for yourself and for someone else at the same time, place two orders. And <strong>subscriptions cannot be gifted</strong> - a subscription bills your card on its cadence and ships to a single address, so the gift option is not offered on any order that contains one. If you want to give someone coffee regularly, buy it for them as separate orders whenever you like.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>

